<article class="env-lemma" id="0CD0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CD0">Lemma <span data-tag="0CD0">53.13.5</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p > 0$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a nonconstant morphism of proper nonsingular curves over $k$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ is smooth, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^0(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = k$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$k(X)/k(Y)$ is purely inseparable. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $Y$ is smooth, $H^0(Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y) = k$, and the genus of $Y$ is equal to the genus of $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0CCZ" data-tag="0CCZ">53.13.4</a> we see that $Y = X^{(p^ n)}$ is the base change of $X$ by $F_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)}^ n$. Thus $Y$ is smooth and the result on the cohomology and genus follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BY9" data-tag="0BY9">53.8.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>